@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il08-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 40 — "נקודות קיצבה וזיכוי בעד ילדים", allowance points and credit for
-- children. Row IL-08. Source lines 1631-1646.
--
-- GAPS.md item 2 of row IL-07: a parent without a spouse has children's credit points under s 40(b),
-- not under s 66(c), which is for spouses. This module answers, for one parent in a tax year, the
-- points s 40(b) gives, paragraph by paragraph, keeping apart the points set against the tax on
-- income from personal exertion ((1A), (1B)) from those set against the tax generally ((1), (2)).
--
-- s 40(a) is a cross-reference to the National Insurance Law; nothing in it is computed here (see
-- its section below). s 40(c) has expired.
--
-- WHO IS ASKED ABOUT. One parent (`A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`), with that parent's
-- children. Where a paragraph turns on the OTHER parent ((1A)'s proviso and condition), the facts
-- about the other parent are fields of the child's record, and the other parent's own answer under
-- (1) is the caller's to supply, from this module asked about that parent (fork F14).
--
-- TAX YEARS. The tables are those amended by תשפ״ג־6 and תשפ״ד־3, in force from tax year 2024 (row
-- IL-02's evidence; ito-il08-tax-years.l4). An earlier year is declined.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 40 — allowance points and credit for children`

§§ `Section 40(a) — allowance points, paid by the National Insurance Institute`

-- src:1632 | (א) יחיד תושב ישראל זכאי לנקודות קיצבה בשל כל אחד מילדיו כקבוע בסעיף 109 לחוק הביטוח הלאומי [נוסח משולב], התשכ״ח–1968; תשלום נקודות הקיצבה ייעשה בידי המוסד לביטוח לאומי לפי חוק הביטוח הלאומי.
-- Not computed. The entitlement is "as fixed in s 109" of the 1968 consolidation of the National
-- Insurance Law, and the Institute pays it under that Law. The present Law's table of old and new
-- section numbers maps the old s 109 to the present s 68 (the child allowance) and Schedule D
-- (National Insurance Law source line 5405), and Schedule D is repealed (that file, line 4518). The
-- present child allowance is fixed in basic amounts, not in allowance points (row IL-06). Whether
-- anyone is "entitled to allowance points under s 40(a)" today is therefore open (fork F19); ss 38 and
-- 39, which turn on it, take it as an input, and s 66(c)(3) gives it to the registered spouse alone
-- (row IL-02).

§§ `Section 40(b)(3) — definitions`

-- src:1641 | (3) לענין סעיף קטן זה –
-- src:1642 | ”ילד להורה אחד“ – ילד שבשנת המס טרם מלאו לו תשע עשרה שנים ואחד מהוריו נפטר בשנת המס או קודם לכן או שהוא רשום במרשם האוכלוסין בלא פרטי אחד ההורים;
-- src:1643 | ”פעוט“ – [note: (נמחקה);]
-- src:1644 | ”שנת לידה“ – שנת המס שבה נולד הילד;
-- src:1645 | ”שנת בגרות“ – שנת המס שבה מלאו לילד שמונה עשרה שנים.
-- Every band of the tables is stated by tax year: the year of birth, "the tax year in which he turned
-- three", the year of majority (18). So the child's age in a tax year is the tax year less the tax
-- year of birth, as row IL-02 reads the same definitions for s 66(c).
@ref ITO s 40(b)(3), lines 1644-1645
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `the child`    IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(3) — the age the child turns in tax year` `the tax year` `:` `the child` MEANS
    `the tax year` MINUS `the child`'s `tax year of birth`

-- "טרם מלאו לו תשע עשרה שנים" in the tax year: had not turned 19 in it, so turns 18 or less (the year of
-- majority is the last year in).
@ref ITO s 40(b)(3), "ילד להורה אחד", line 1642
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `the child`    IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(b)(3) — a child of one parent, in tax year` `the tax year` `:` `the child` MEANS
        `the age` AT LEAST 0 AND `the age` AT MOST 18
    AND (    `the child`'s `the other parent died in or before the tax year`
         OR  `the child`'s `registered in the population register without the details of one parent`)
    WHERE `the age` MEANS `s 40(b)(3) — the age the child turns in tax year` `the tax year` `:` `the child`

§§ `Section 40(b)(1) — a parent in a single-parent family`

-- src:1633 | (ב)(1) בחישוב המס של יחיד תושב ישראל שהוא הורה במשפחה חד־הורית שהיו לו ילדים שבשנת המס טרם מלאו להם תשע־עשרה שנה ושכלכלתם היתה עליו, אך אינו זכאי לנקודת זיכוי לפי סעיף 37, יובאו בחשבון, בנוסף לנקודות הקיצבה לפי סעיף קטן (א), בשל ילדיו כאמור הנמצאים אצלו, 2 1 ⁄ 2 נקודות זיכוי בשל כל ילד בשנת לידתו ו־ 1 ⁄ 2 נקודת זיכוי בשל כל ילד בשנת בגרותו, 4 1 ⁄ 2 נקודות זיכוי בשל כל ילד החל בשנת המס שלאחר לידתו ועד לשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שנתיים, 3 1 ⁄ 2 נקודות זיכוי בשל כל ילד בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שלוש שנים, 2 1 ⁄ 2 נקודות זיכוי בשל כל ילד בשנות המס שבהן מלאו לו ארבע שנים וחמש שנים ושתי נקודות זיכוי בשל כל ילד החל בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שש שנים ועד לשנת המס שקדמה לשנת בגרותו.

-- The table of (1), in the source's order. The bands are disjoint, so the order decides nothing.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1), line 1633
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(1) — the credit points for a child who turns` `the age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the age` EQUALS 0                              THEN 2.5
        IF   `the age` EQUALS 18                             THEN 0.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 1 AND `the age` AT MOST 2    THEN 4.5
        IF   `the age` EQUALS 3                              THEN 3.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 4 AND `the age` AT MOST 5    THEN 2.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 6 AND `the age` AT MOST 17   THEN 2
        OTHERWISE                                                 0

-- The parent's limbs: a resident individual, a parent in a single-parent family, not entitled to a
-- point under s 37.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1), line 1633
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(b)(1) — the parent's own conditions are met, for` p MEANS
        p's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
    AND p's `a parent in a single-parent family`
    AND NOT p's `entitled to a credit point under section 37`

-- The child's limbs: had not turned 19 in the tax year, maintained by the parent, and with him.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1), line 1633
GIVEN p           IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(b)(1) — the parent has credit points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` MEANS
        `s 40(b)(1) — the parent's own conditions are met, for` p
    AND `the age` AT LEAST 0 AND `the age` AT MOST 18
    AND `the child`'s `the parent maintained the child`
    AND `the child`'s `the child is with the parent`
    WHERE `the age` MEANS `s 40(b)(3) — the age the child turns in tax year` (p's `tax year`) `:` `the child`

-- "שהיו לו ילדים", and the points "בשל ילדיו כאמור": entitled under (1) where he has points for at
-- least one child. (1B) and (2) turn on this.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1), line 1633
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(b)(1) — the parent is entitled to credit points under paragraph (1), for` p MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD `s 40(b)(1) — the parent has credit points for the child, for` p `:` c) (p's `children`)

§§ `Section 40(b)(1A) — the father of a child in a single-parent family`

-- src:1634 | (1א) בחישוב המס של יחיד תושב ישראל שהוא אב לילד במשפחה חד־הורית ואינו זכאי לנקודות זיכוי לפי פסקה (1), יובאו בחשבון, כנגד המס החל על הכנסתו מיגיעה אישית, בשל כל ילד כאמור, נקודות זיכוי כמפורט להלן, ואולם אם אמו של הילד במשפחה חד־הורית היא תושבת ישראל ואינה זכאית, בשל אותו ילד, לנקודות זיכוי לפי פסקה (1), יובאו בחשבון נקודות הזיכוי לפי פסקת משנה זו, כנגד הכנסתה מיגיעה אישית, ולא כנגד הכנסתו של האב:
-- src:1635 | (א) 2 1 ⁄ 2 נקודות זיכוי בשנת לידתו של הילד;
-- src:1636 | (ב) 4 1 ⁄ 2 נקודות זיכוי בשל כל ילד החל בשנת המס שלאחר לידתו ועד לשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שנתיים, 3 1 ⁄ 2 נקודות זיכוי בשל כל ילד בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שלוש שנים ו־2 1 ⁄ 2 נקודות זיכוי בשל כל ילד בשנות המס שבהן מלאו לו ארבע שנים וחמש שנים;
-- src:1637 | (ג) נקודת זיכוי אחת בשל כל ילד החל בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שש שנים ועד לשנת המס שקדמה לשנת בגרותו.

-- The table of (1A), (a)-(c). No row for the year of majority: (c) ends with the year before it.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1A)(a)-(c), lines 1635-1637
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(1A) — the credit points for a child who turns` `the age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the age` EQUALS 0                              THEN 2.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 1 AND `the age` AT MOST 2    THEN 4.5
        IF   `the age` EQUALS 3                              THEN 3.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 4 AND `the age` AT MOST 5    THEN 2.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 6 AND `the age` AT MOST 17   THEN 1
        OTHERWISE                                                 0

-- The father's limbs: a resident, the father of a child in a single-parent family, "not entitled to
-- credit points under (1)" (fork F15, below). The proviso moves the points to the mother where she is
-- a resident and has no points for the child under (1) ("בשל אותו ילד": for that child, by the text).
-- Version 0.5.0 (fork F15, inventory 08i-F15). The father's limb does not say "for that child", as
-- the mother's does; versions 0.1.0 to 0.4.0 read it for that child only. RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08
-- (SHRUG): a switch (nouns, `A reading of section 40(b)(1A), "not entitled to credit points under
-- paragraph (1)"`): for that child; for any child; and by default declined where the two readings
-- give different answers. The readings part only for a father who has (1) points for some child and
-- a child in a single-parent family who is not with him.
-- `for that child alone` below is TRUE for the first reading, FALSE for the second.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1A), line 1634; fork F15
GIVEN p                       IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `the child`             IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
      `for that child alone`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(b)(1A) — the father has the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` `for that child alone` MEANS
        `the child`'s `the parent is` EQUALS `the father of the child`
    AND p's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
    AND `the child`'s `in a single-parent family`
    AND NOT (IF   `for that child alone`
             THEN `s 40(b)(1) — the parent has credit points for the child, for` p `:` `the child`
             ELSE `s 40(b)(1) — the parent is entitled to credit points under paragraph (1), for` p)
    AND NOT (    `the child`'s `the other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`
             AND NOT `the child`'s `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`)

-- The mother takes them where the father would have had them but for the proviso: the father is a
-- resident without points under (1) (fork F15: for that child, or for any child, the second read from
-- the children on her record, an input convention: nouns), and she is a resident without points for
-- the child under (1).
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1A), proviso, line 1634; fork F15
GIVEN p                       IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `the child`             IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
      `for that child alone`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(b)(1A) — the mother has the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` `for that child alone` MEANS
        `the child`'s `the parent is` EQUALS `the mother of the child`
    AND p's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
    AND `the child`'s `in a single-parent family`
    AND NOT `s 40(b)(1) — the parent has credit points for the child, for` p `:` `the child`
    AND `the child`'s `the other parent is an Israeli resident in the tax year`
    AND NOT (IF   `for that child alone`
             THEN `the child`'s `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`
             ELSE any (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`) (p's `children`))

@ref ITO s 40(b)(1A), line 1634; fork F15
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 40(b)(1A) does not say whether the father is to be not entitled under paragraph (1) for that child or for any child, and here it decides` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 40(b)(1A) does not say whether the father is to be not entitled under paragraph (1) for that child or for any child, and here it decides"

-- By the version 0.1.0 names, at the default: declined where the readings differ.
GIVEN p           IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(b)(1A) — the father has the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` MEANS
    IF   `for that child` EQUALS `for any child`
    THEN `for that child`
    ELSE `section 40(b)(1A) does not say whether the father is to be not entitled under paragraph (1) for that child or for any child, and here it decides`
    WHERE
        `for that child` MEANS `s 40(b)(1A) — the father has the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` TRUE
        `for any child`  MEANS `s 40(b)(1A) — the father has the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` FALSE

GIVEN p           IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(b)(1A) — the mother has the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` MEANS
    IF   `for that child` EQUALS `for any child`
    THEN `for that child`
    ELSE `section 40(b)(1A) does not say whether the father is to be not entitled under paragraph (1) for that child or for any child, and here it decides`
    WHERE
        `for that child` MEANS `s 40(b)(1A) — the mother has the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` TRUE
        `for any child`  MEANS `s 40(b)(1A) — the mother has the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` FALSE

§§ `Section 40(b)(1A1) — the mother's election`

-- src:1638 | (1א1) על אף האמור בפסקאות (1) ו־(1א), אמו של ילד תהיה זכאית לבחור אם נקודת זיכוי אחת מתוך נקודות הזיכוי שלהן היא זכאית כאמור באותן פסקאות, לפי העניין, בשנת הלידה, תובא בחשבון בשנת המס שבה נולד הילד או בשנת המס שלאחריה.
-- One of the mother's birth-year points, under (1) or (1A), counted in the next tax year instead.
-- As row IL-02 reads the same words in s 66(c)(4)(a1): one point less in the year of birth, one more
-- in the year after.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1A1), line 1638
GIVEN `the child`       IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
      `the age`         IS A NUMBER
      `the points`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(1A1) — the mother's points for` `the child` `, aged` `the age` `, from a table giving` `the points` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `elected` AND `the age` EQUALS 0 THEN `the points` MINUS 1
        IF   `elected` AND `the age` EQUALS 1 THEN `the points` PLUS 1
        OTHERWISE `the points`
    WHERE `elected` MEANS     `the child`'s `the parent is` EQUALS `the mother of the child`
                          AND `the child`'s `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year`

§§ `Section 40(b)(1B) — a child of one parent`

-- src:1639 | (1ב) במשפחה חד־הורית שבה ילד להורה אחד ואותו הורה זכאי לנקודות זיכוי לפי פסקה (1), תובא בחשבון כנגד הכנסתו מיגיעה אישית של אותו הורה, נקודת זיכוי אחת נוספת; וכן יובאו בחשבון כנגד הכנסתו של ההורה כאמור, על אף הוראות פסקה (1א), גם נקודות הזיכוי לפי אותה פסקה.
-- Where a child of one parent has points from this parent under (1): one further point, once for the
-- family (fork F16), and the (1A) table's points for that child, which no other parent can take.
-- Both are set against the tax on the parent's income from personal exertion (fork F17).
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1B), line 1639
GIVEN p           IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40(b)(1B) — a child of one parent for whom the parent has points under paragraph (1), for` p `:` `the child` MEANS
        `s 40(b)(3) — a child of one parent, in tax year` (p's `tax year`) `:` `the child`
    AND `s 40(b)(1) — the parent has credit points for the child, for` p `:` `the child`

-- One child's (1A)-table points under (1B)'s second limb.
-- Version 0.2.0 (OB1). (1A1) moves "נקודת זיכוי אחת", one point, of the birth-year points the mother
-- is entitled to under (1) and (1A). A child of one parent has (1B)'s (1A) points only where the
-- parent has (1) points for it, so the mother of such a child always has (1) points to move it from;
-- the move is made once, in (1) (`s 40(b)(1) — the points for the child, for`), and not again here.
-- Version 0.1.0 applied it here too, so two points moved: for a child born in 2025 the mother had
-- 6 points in 2025 and 10 in 2026 without the election, and 4 and 12 with it; now 5 and 11. Taking
-- the point from (1) rather than from these points changes no total, only whether the moved point is
-- set against the tax generally or the tax on income from personal exertion (fork F13, version 0.2.0;
-- assumed, not ruled).
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1B), line 1639; s 40(b)(1A1), line 1638
GIVEN p           IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(1B) — the paragraph (1A) points for a child of one parent, for` p `:` `the child` MEANS
    IF   `s 40(b)(1B) — a child of one parent for whom the parent has points under paragraph (1), for` p `:` `the child`
    THEN `s 40(b)(1A) — the credit points for a child who turns` `the age`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE `the age` MEANS `s 40(b)(3) — the age the child turns in tax year` (p's `tax year`) `:` `the child`

-- Version 0.5.0 (fork F16, inventory 08i-F15). "נקודת זיכוי אחת נוספת": once (versions 0.1.0 to
-- 0.4.0), or once for each child of one parent for whom the parent has (1) points. RULED by Meng on
-- 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): a switch (nouns, `A reading of section 40(b)(1B) and (2), "one further credit
-- point"`), the same for (2)'s further point, declining by default where the readings differ: where
-- there are two or more such children. `once` below is TRUE for the first reading.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1B), line 1639; fork F16
GIVEN p      IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `once` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(1B) — the credit points, for` p `, the further point given once:` `once` MEANS
    IF   `the children of one parent` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN     (IF `once` THEN 1 ELSE `the children of one parent`)
        PLUS sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD `s 40(b)(1B) — the paragraph (1A) points for a child of one parent, for` p `:` c) (p's `children`))
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the children of one parent` MEANS
            sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD IF `s 40(b)(1B) — a child of one parent for whom the parent has points under paragraph (1), for` p `:` c THEN 1 ELSE 0) (p's `children`))

@ref ITO s 40(b)(1B), (2), lines 1639-1640; fork F16
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 40(b)(1B) and (2) do not say whether the one further credit point is given once or for each child, and here it decides` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 40(b)(1B) and (2) do not say whether the one further credit point is given once or for each child, and here it decides"

-- By the version 0.1.0 name, at the default.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1B), line 1639; fork F16
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(1B) — the credit points, for` p MEANS
    IF   `s 40(b)(1B) — the credit points, for` p `, the further point given once:` TRUE
         EQUALS `s 40(b)(1B) — the credit points, for` p `, the further point given once:` FALSE
    THEN `s 40(b)(1B) — the credit points, for` p `, the further point given once:` TRUE
    ELSE `section 40(b)(1B) and (2) do not say whether the one further credit point is given once or for each child, and here it decides`

§§ `Section 40(b)(2) — parents living apart`

-- src:1640 | (2) הורים החיים בנפרד יקבל ההורה הזכאי לנקודת זיכוי לפי פסקה (1), נקודת זיכוי אחת נוספת ואם כלכלת ילדיהם מחולקת ביניהם, יקבל ההורה שאינו זכאי לנקודת זיכוי על פי פסקה (1) נקודת זיכוי אחת או חלק ממנה לפי חלקו בהוצאות הכלכלה.
-- The parent entitled under (1): one further point (once, fork F16). The other parent, where the
-- children's maintenance is divided: one point, or the part of it that is his share of the
-- maintenance expenses. The paragraph has no residence limb (fork F18).
--
-- Version 0.3.0 (the capstone's second independent pass, observation O1). Versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 gave the
-- second limb's point to any parent not entitled under (1) who bore a share of the maintenance, up to
-- the whole of it, resident or not, whoever the other parent was: a non-resident father bearing all
-- of it, the children's other parent abroad, had 1 point. Against the text:
--   "ואם כלכלת ילדיהם מחולקת ביניהם": only where the maintenance is divided between the parents. A
--     parent who bears all of it, or none, does not share it: no point under the second limb. The
--     text decides this; versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 were wrong for a share of 1.
--   Residence: (1) and (1A) are each for "יחיד תושב ישראל"; (2) does not say, and the Chapter gives no
--     general answer. Fork F18, which versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 took as "no condition", is now declined where it
--     matters: a parent who is not an Israeli resident and whom the second limb would credit.
--   "ההורה שאינו זכאי לנקודת זיכוי על פי פסקה (1)" is set against "ההורה הזכאי" of the first limb:
--     whether the second limb reaches a parent where the other parent is not entitled under (1)
--     either, the text does not say (fork F37). Declined where it matters: the second limb would
--     credit the parent, and the other parent has (1) points for none of the children (the field on
--     each child's record, fork F14).
@ref ITO s 40(b)(2), line 1640: whether the second limb reaches a parent who is not an Israeli resident (fork F18)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 40(b)(2) does not say whether its point for a share of the maintenance goes to a parent who is not an Israeli resident` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 40(b)(2) does not say whether its point for a share of the maintenance goes to a parent who is not an Israeli resident"

@ref ITO s 40(b)(2), line 1640: whether the second limb reaches a parent where neither parent is entitled under paragraph (1) (fork F37)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 40(b)(2) does not say whether its point for a share of the maintenance goes to a parent where the other parent is not entitled under paragraph (1) either` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 40(b)(2) does not say whether its point for a share of the maintenance goes to a parent where the other parent is not entitled under paragraph (1) either"

@ref ITO s 40(b)(2), line 1640; fork F16 (version 0.5.0) for the further point of the first limb
GIVEN p      IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `once` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(2) — the credit points, for` p `, the further point given once:` `once` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   NOT p's `living apart from the other parent`
        THEN 0
        IF   `s 40(b)(1) — the parent is entitled to credit points under paragraph (1), for` p
        THEN IF `once` THEN 1 ELSE sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD IF `s 40(b)(1) — the parent has credit points for the child, for` p `:` c THEN 1 ELSE 0) (p's `children`))
        IF   NOT (`the share` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the share` LESS THAN 1)
        THEN 0
        IF   NOT p's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
        THEN `section 40(b)(2) does not say whether its point for a share of the maintenance goes to a parent who is not an Israeli resident`
        IF   NOT any (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the other parent has credit points for the child under paragraph (1)`) (p's `children`)
        THEN `section 40(b)(2) does not say whether its point for a share of the maintenance goes to a parent where the other parent is not entitled under paragraph (1) either`
        OTHERWISE `the share`
    WHERE `the share` MEANS p's `share of the children's maintenance expenses borne`

-- By the version 0.1.0 name, at the default.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(2), line 1640; fork F16
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(2) — the credit points, for` p MEANS
    IF   `s 40(b)(2) — the credit points, for` p `, the further point given once:` TRUE
         EQUALS `s 40(b)(2) — the credit points, for` p `, the further point given once:` FALSE
    THEN `s 40(b)(2) — the credit points, for` p `, the further point given once:` TRUE
    ELSE `section 40(b)(1B) and (2) do not say whether the one further credit point is given once or for each child, and here it decides`

§§ `Section 40(b) — the points, paragraph by paragraph`

DECLARE `Credit points under section 40(b)` HAS
    `under paragraph (1), with the election of (1A1)`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `under paragraph (1A), with the election of (1A1), against the tax on income from personal exertion` IS A NUMBER
    `under paragraph (1B), against the tax on income from personal exertion`                  IS A NUMBER
    `under paragraph (2)`                                                                     IS A NUMBER

-- One child's points under (1), and under (1A), for the parent asked about.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1), (1A), (1A1), lines 1633-1638
GIVEN p           IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(1) — the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` MEANS
    IF   `s 40(b)(1) — the parent has credit points for the child, for` p `:` `the child`
    THEN `s 40(b)(1A1) — the mother's points for` `the child` `, aged` `the age` `, from a table giving` (`s 40(b)(1) — the credit points for a child who turns` `the age`)
    ELSE 0
    WHERE `the age` MEANS `s 40(b)(3) — the age the child turns in tax year` (p's `tax year`) `:` `the child`

@ref ITO s 40(b)(1A), (1A1), lines 1634-1638; fork F15
GIVEN p                      IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `the child`            IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
      `for that child alone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(1A) — the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` `for that child alone` MEANS
    IF   `s 40(b)(1A) — the father has the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` `for that child alone`
      OR `s 40(b)(1A) — the mother has the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` `for that child alone`
    THEN `s 40(b)(1A1) — the mother's points for` `the child` `, aged` `the age` `, from a table giving` (`s 40(b)(1A) — the credit points for a child who turns` `the age`)
    ELSE 0
    WHERE `the age` MEANS `s 40(b)(3) — the age the child turns in tax year` (p's `tax year`) `:` `the child`

-- By the version 0.1.0 name, at the default.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1A), (1A1), lines 1634-1638; fork F15
GIVEN p           IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b)(1A) — the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` MEANS
    IF   `for that child` EQUALS `for any child`
    THEN `for that child`
    ELSE `section 40(b)(1A) does not say whether the father is to be not entitled under paragraph (1) for that child or for any child, and here it decides`
    WHERE
        `for that child` MEANS `s 40(b)(1A) — the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` TRUE
        `for any child`  MEANS `s 40(b)(1A) — the points for the child, for` p `:` `the child` `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` FALSE

-- The four paragraphs under one choice of each reading (F15: for that child alone or not; F16: the
-- further point once or not).
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1)-(2), lines 1633-1640; forks F15, F16
GIVEN p                      IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `for that child alone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `once`                 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Credit points under section 40(b)`
`s 40(b) — the credit points, paragraph by paragraph, for` p `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` `for that child alone` `, the further point given once:` `once` MEANS
    `Credit points under section 40(b)` WITH
        `under paragraph (1), with the election of (1A1)`                                         IS sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD `s 40(b)(1) — the points for the child, for` p `:` c) (p's `children`))
        `under paragraph (1A), with the election of (1A1), against the tax on income from personal exertion` IS sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD `s 40(b)(1A) — the points for the child, for` p `:` c `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` `for that child alone`) (p's `children`))
        `under paragraph (1B), against the tax on income from personal exertion`                  IS `s 40(b)(1B) — the credit points, for` p `, the further point given once:` `once`
        `under paragraph (2)`                                                                     IS `s 40(b)(2) — the credit points, for` p `, the further point given once:` `once`

§§ `Section 40(b) — the switches for forks F15 and F16 (version 0.5.0)`

-- RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): one switch for each fork, both at the default, which declines
-- where the fork's readings give different answers to the question asked (a paragraph's points, the
-- points against the tax generally or on income from personal exertion, or all of them), and answers
-- where they agree. Each other reading is kept by name (nouns) and tested.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1A), (1B), (2), lines 1634-1640; forks F15, F16; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `The readings of section 40(b)`
`section 40(b) — the readings this row takes` MEANS
    `The readings of section 40(b)` WITH
        `paragraph (1A), not entitled under paragraph (1)` IS `declined where the reading of paragraph (1A) decides`
        `paragraphs (1B) and (2), one further point`       IS `declined where the reading of paragraphs (1B) and (2) decides`

-- The questions a caller may ask of s 40(b).
DECLARE `Which credit points under section 40(b)` IS ONE OF
    `the points under paragraph (1)`
    `the points under paragraph (1A)`
    `the points under paragraph (1B)`
    `the points under paragraph (2)`
    `the points set against the tax generally`
    `the points set against the tax on income from personal exertion`
    `all the points`

GIVEN `points` IS A `Credit points under section 40(b)`
      `which`  IS A `Which credit points under section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b) — of the points` `points` `, those asked:` `which` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which`
    WHEN `the points under paragraph (1)`  THEN `(1)`
    WHEN `the points under paragraph (1A)` THEN `(1A)`
    WHEN `the points under paragraph (1B)` THEN `(1B)`
    WHEN `the points under paragraph (2)`  THEN `(2)`
    WHEN `the points set against the tax generally` THEN `(1)` PLUS `(2)`
    WHEN `the points set against the tax on income from personal exertion` THEN `(1A)` PLUS `(1B)`
    WHEN `all the points` THEN `(1)` PLUS `(1A)` PLUS `(1B)` PLUS `(2)`
    WHERE
        `(1)`  MEANS `points`'s `under paragraph (1), with the election of (1A1)`
        `(1A)` MEANS `points`'s `under paragraph (1A), with the election of (1A1), against the tax on income from personal exertion`
        `(1B)` MEANS `points`'s `under paragraph (1B), against the tax on income from personal exertion`
        `(2)`  MEANS `points`'s `under paragraph (2)`

-- F16 at a reading, F15 fixed.
GIVEN `which`                IS A `Which credit points under section 40(b)`
      p                      IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      `for that child alone` IS A BOOLEAN
      y                      IS A `A reading of section 40(b)(1B) and (2), "one further credit point"`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b) — the points asked,` `which` `, for` p `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` `for that child alone` `, reading the further point as` y MEANS
    CONSIDER y
    WHEN `once`                THEN `given once`
    WHEN `once for each child` THEN `given for each child`
    WHEN `declined where the reading of paragraphs (1B) and (2) decides`
        THEN IF   `given once` EQUALS `given for each child`
             THEN `given once`
             ELSE `section 40(b)(1B) and (2) do not say whether the one further credit point is given once or for each child, and here it decides`
    WHERE
        `given once`           MEANS `s 40(b) — of the points` (`s 40(b) — the credit points, paragraph by paragraph, for` p `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` `for that child alone` `, the further point given once:` TRUE) `, those asked:` `which`
        `given for each child` MEANS `s 40(b) — of the points` (`s 40(b) — the credit points, paragraph by paragraph, for` p `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` `for that child alone` `, the further point given once:` FALSE) `, those asked:` `which`

-- Both forks at their readings.
@ref ITO s 40(b), lines 1633-1640; forks F15, F16
GIVEN `which` IS A `Which credit points under section 40(b)`
      p       IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      r       IS A `The readings of section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 40(b) — the points asked,` `which` `, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `paragraph (1A), not entitled under paragraph (1)`
    WHEN `for that child` THEN `for that child`
    WHEN `for any child`  THEN `for any child`
    WHEN `declined where the reading of paragraph (1A) decides`
        THEN IF   `for that child` EQUALS `for any child`
             THEN `for that child`
             ELSE `section 40(b)(1A) does not say whether the father is to be not entitled under paragraph (1) for that child or for any child, and here it decides`
    WHERE
        y                MEANS r's `paragraphs (1B) and (2), one further point`
        `for that child` MEANS `s 40(b) — the points asked,` `which` `, for` p `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` TRUE `, reading the further point as` y
        `for any child`  MEANS `s 40(b) — the points asked,` `which` `, for` p `, "not entitled under (1)" read for that child alone:` FALSE `, reading the further point as` y

-- The four paragraphs at the readings, each answered or declined on its own (a record's fields are
-- evaluated only when asked for).
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1)-(2), lines 1633-1640; forks F15, F16
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      r IS A `The readings of section 40(b)`
GIVETH A `Credit points under section 40(b)`
`s 40(b) — the credit points, paragraph by paragraph, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r MEANS
    `Credit points under section 40(b)` WITH
        `under paragraph (1), with the election of (1A1)`                                         IS `s 40(b) — the points asked,` `the points under paragraph (1)` `, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r
        `under paragraph (1A), with the election of (1A1), against the tax on income from personal exertion` IS `s 40(b) — the points asked,` `the points under paragraph (1A)` `, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r
        `under paragraph (1B), against the tax on income from personal exertion`                  IS `s 40(b) — the points asked,` `the points under paragraph (1B)` `, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r
        `under paragraph (2)`                                                                     IS `s 40(b) — the points asked,` `the points under paragraph (2)` `, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r

-- By the version 0.1.0 name, at the default.
@ref ITO s 40(b)(1)-(2), lines 1633-1640
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A `Credit points under section 40(b)`
`s 40(b) — the credit points, paragraph by paragraph, for` p MEANS
    `s 40(b) — the credit points, paragraph by paragraph, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` `section 40(b) — the readings this row takes`

-- s 48A: s 40(b) gives credits of this Chapter, so the 2014 Regulations may take them from a
-- foreign worker; declined where the section would give him any (as for ss 34-36A in row IL-01).
@ref ITO s 48A, lines 1810-1812 — not encoded in this row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`row IL-08, section 40(b): section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"

-- The tax years and s 48A, around any answer of s 40(b) for the parent.
GIVEN a       IS A TYPE
      p       IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      r       IS A `The readings of section 40(b)`
      `answer` IS AN a
GIVETH AN a
`for the parent` p `, at the readings` r `, after the tax years and section 48A:` `answer` MEANS
    `for tax year` (p's `tax year`) `, row IL-08 answers`
        (IF   p's `a foreign worker` AND `s 40(b) — the points asked,` `all the points` `, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `row IL-08, section 40(b): section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded`
         ELSE `answer`)

@ref ITO s 40(b), lines 1633-1645; s 48A, line 1811; forks F15, F16
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      r IS A `The readings of section 40(b)`
GIVETH A `Credit points under section 40(b)`
`the credit points under section 40(b) for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r MEANS
    `for the parent` p `, at the readings` r `, after the tax years and section 48A:` (`s 40(b) — the credit points, paragraph by paragraph, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r)

@export The credit points under Income Tax Ordinance s 40(b) for one parent's children in a tax year from 2024, split into points set against the tax generally ((1), (2)) and points set against the tax on income from personal exertion ((1A), (1B)); each declines where forks F15 (paragraph (1A) for that child or any child) or F16 (the further point of (1B) and (2) once or for each child) change it
@ref ITO s 40(b), lines 1633-1645; s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
          @desc the parent (residence, single-parent family, s 37 entitlement, living apart, share of maintenance) and each child (tax year of birth, father or mother, maintained, with the parent, single-parent family, child of one parent, the mother's election, the other parent's residence and paragraph (1) points)
GIVETH A `Credit points under section 40(b)`
`the credit points under section 40(b) for` p MEANS
    `the credit points under section 40(b) for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` `section 40(b) — the readings this row takes`

@ref ITO s 40(b)(1), (2); forks F15, F16
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      r IS A `The readings of section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r MEANS
    `for the parent` p `, at the readings` r `, after the tax years and section 48A:` (`s 40(b) — the points asked,` `the points set against the tax generally` `, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r)

@ref ITO s 40(b)(1A), (1B); forks F15, F16
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      r IS A `The readings of section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r MEANS
    `for the parent` p `, at the readings` r `, after the tax years and section 48A:` (`s 40(b) — the points asked,` `the points set against the tax on income from personal exertion` `, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r)

@ref ITO s 40(b); forks F15, F16
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
      r IS A `The readings of section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 40(b) in all, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r MEANS
    `for the parent` p `, at the readings` r `, after the tax years and section 48A:` (`s 40(b) — the points asked,` `all the points` `, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` r)

-- By the version 0.1.0 names, at the default.
GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` p MEANS
    `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax generally, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` `section 40(b) — the readings this row takes`

GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` p MEANS
    `the credit points under section 40(b) set against the tax on income from personal exertion, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` `section 40(b) — the readings this row takes`

GIVEN p IS A `A parent in a tax year, for section 40(b)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 40(b) in all, for` p MEANS
    `the credit points under section 40(b) in all, for` p `, reading section 40(b) as` `section 40(b) — the readings this row takes`

§§ `Section 40(c) — expired`
-- src:1646 | (ג) [note: (פקע).]
